# Standard icon pack (`IOS_ICONS`)

The project's shared icon set lives in **`public/admin/admin-ui.js`** as `IOS_ICONS` (Lucide-style stroke SVGs, `currentColor`). Helpers: `createIosIconBtn`, `createAgentBtn`, `agentIconSvg`.

## Always reuse — never invent

Before adding any icon (toolbar button, header control, panel action, empty state, map node chrome, etc.):

1. Check whether the key already exists on `IOS_ICONS`.
2. If it does, use that SVG (or `createIosIconBtn({ iconKey })` in admin client JS).
3. If it does not, **add the icon to `IOS_ICONS` first**, then consume it. Do not paste a one-off SVG elsewhere and leave the pack incomplete.
4. Do not freestyle filled / alternate shapes when a pack glyph exists or belongs in the pack. Match the existing stroke style (`fill="none"`, `stroke="currentColor"`, `stroke-width="1.75"` unless neighbors differ).

## Astro / SSR markup

Astro components cannot import the admin client module. When an icon must appear in Astro markup (e.g. `Header.astro`):

- Copy the **exact** SVG string from `IOS_ICONS.<key>`.
- Leave an HTML comment pointing at the pack key (e.g. `<!-- IOS_ICONS.bell — keep in sync with public/admin/admin-ui.js -->`).
- If you change the pack glyph, update every inlined copy in the same change.

## Do not

- Hand-draw or AI-generate a new bell / trash / share / etc. when the pack already has one (or should get one).
- Introduce a second icon library (Heroicons, Phosphor, Material, emoji-as-UI) for chrome that `IOS_ICONS` covers.
- Use filled solid variants that break visual consistency with the stroke set.

Brand logos (Simple Icons / company SVG) and photographic assets are separate — this rule is for UI chrome icons.
